{
  "stem": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Ethanoic acid is mixed with ethanol."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The ethanol is contaminated with a small amount of methanol."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The following equilibria are established."
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "latex": "\\text{CH}_3\\text{CO}_2\\text{H(l)} + \\text{CH}_3\\text{CH}_2\\text{OH(l)} \\rightleftharpoons \\text{CH}_3\\text{CO}_2\\text{CH}_2\\text{CH}_3\\text{(l)} + \\text{H}_2\\text{O(l)} \\qquad K_\\text{c} = K_1"
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "latex": "\\text{CH}_3\\text{CO}_2\\text{H(l)} + \\text{CH}_3\\text{OH(l)} \\rightleftharpoons \\text{CH}_3\\text{CO}_2\\text{CH}_3\\text{(l)} + \\text{H}_2\\text{O(l)} \\qquad K_\\text{c} = K_2"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Which statement about the equilibrium mixture is correct?"
    }
  ],
  "layout": "list",
  "options": {
    "A": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Only ethyl ethanoate will be formed because there is much more ethanol present than methanol."
      }
    ],
    "B": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "In this mixture $\\dfrac{[\\text{CH}_3\\text{CO}_2\\text{CH}_2\\text{CH}_3]}{[\\text{CH}_3\\text{CO}_2\\text{CH}_3]} = \\dfrac{K_1}{K_2}$."
      }
    ],
    "C": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Adding water to the mixture will alter the mole ratio of the two esters."
      }
    ],
    "D": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Adding methyl ethanoate to the mixture will increase the number of moles of ethyl ethanoate."
      }
    ]
  }
